// GENERATED by tools/hdmi_modes.py amiga-gen - do not edit. T164 WP1: the 9 HDMI modes of the host (all cores).
// T188 edition (cores/amiga, cores/amiga1200 only): rows 0, 1, 2 (576p, 720p, 1080p at 50 Hz) have the raster and the CDCE ratio at which one HDMI
// frame is the Amiga frame (dot4x x 9/10 / (8 x 227 x 313)) within 1 ppm. Row 2 has no hm_cdce_lock (a frame-buffer core's row).
// T234: rows 12, 13, 14 are the host's own rows 0, 1, 2 (576p, 720p, 1080p at 50 Hz, the rows of before T188). mode_req.v maps a request for row 0..2 to
// them while the setting Frame follow is Off (the default), hdmi_timing does not follow the core on them; a request is still refused above 11 and the
// status register reports the requested row (0..2), never 12..14.
// mode index m = family * 6 + hdmi: family 0 = 50 Hz, 1 = 60 Hz; hdmi 0 576p/480p, 1 720p, 2 1080p, 3 800x600, 4 1024x768, 5 1280x1024
// the 50 Hz PC rows (3, 4, 5) do not exist (Q5): hm_valid is 0 and every other function answers 0 for them
